---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
const updated = '2026-05-27'
---
<Base title="Now · Ashish Kshirsagar">
  <main>
    <p class="mono" style="font-size: var(--small);"><a href="/">← home</a></p>
    <header style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h1>now</h1>
      <p class="mono muted" style="font-size: var(--small);">
        updated {updated} · <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener">what is a now page?</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <h2>building</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Portfolio v2</strong> — rebuilding this site as an Astro multi-persona static build. The chrome, the routing, the receipts — all in the open.</li>
        <li><strong>IODevz exploration</strong> — three-founder collective. My current direction is an MCP Gateway in Go: one routable endpoint, many MCP servers behind it.</li>
        <li><strong>OpenCode setup</strong> — pruning the agent fleet down to what earns its keep. Orchestrator-first, capability-named, no committee.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <h2>learning</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>How Cloudflare KV's TTL semantics compose with index keys. Short answer: TTL on data keys + capped LRU on index keys = a clean rolling-window event store with no cron.</li>
        <li>How to draw boundaries between agents without it becoming a committee. The interesting failures are at the seams.</li>
        <li>Hindustani classical — not playing, just listening. Building taste.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <h2>avoiding</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Letting agents merge their own PRs without a diff review.</li>
        <li>Adding new tools before retiring the last one that didn't earn its place.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <hr />
    <footer class="mono" style="font-size: var(--tiny); color: var(--fg-faint); text-align: center;">
      <a href="/">home</a> · <a href="/writing">writing</a> · <a href="/projects">projects</a> · <a href="/feed">feed</a> · <a href="/uses">uses</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
  <style>
    main ul { padding-left: 1.5rem; }
    main li { margin: 0.5rem 0; line-height: 1.6; }
    main strong { color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
</Base>
